<a href="https://app.tvtime.com">TV Time</a>, the popular show and movie tracking app, is shutting down on July 15, with all personal user data set to be deleted after that date.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/07/tv-time-app.jpeg" alt="" width="1920" height="1080" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1054866" /><br/>
In a <a href="https://whipmedia.freshdesk.com/support/solutions/articles/68000029988-tv-time-is-shutting-down">support page update</a> announcing the news, the company admitted that it was "no longer sustainable to continue operating the service as a free app," and said that there was "not enough demand for a paid app."<br/>
<br/>
Come the shutdown date, the TV Time app will be removed from both the App Store and Google Play, and the tvtime.com website will go offline permanently.<br/>
<br/>
Users who want to preserve their viewing history and tracked data can request an export through the app's <a href="https://gdpr.tvtime.com/gdpr/self-service">GDPR self-service tool</a> before the July 15 cutoff. The company says all personal user data will be deleted after that date, but it may retain aggregated, non-personal data for business or legal purposes.<br/>
<br/>
